cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Maieusis, please cite it. The DOI recorded here is the concept DOI,
  which represents the software across versions and always resolves to the latest
  release. When you need to report the exact version you ran, use that release's
  version DOI instead; the citation guide lists both.
type: software
title: "Maieusis"
abstract: >-
  An agent-operated scientific question-development system that transfers
  source-backed question-forming patterns and evaluates whether proposed
  question families can be responsibly planned through inspection of a real
  target dataset before scientific analysis.
authors:
  - family-names: "Xu"
    given-names: "Yunlong"
    alias: "Draco (Yunlong) Xu"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2589-7232"
    affiliation: "University of Chicago"
  - family-names: "Doiron"
    given-names: "Brent"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6916-5511"
version: "0.1.1"
date-released: 2026-08-07
# Concept DOI, deliberately, not a version DOI. A version DOI does not exist until Zenodo mints it
# from the published GitHub Release, while the release workflow validates this file during the
# freeze that precedes publication -- so a version DOI here could only ever be invented or stale.
# The concept DOI is true at every point in that sequence and resolves to the latest release.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21388805"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/BeibaiDraco/maieusis"
keywords:
  - "AI for science"
  - "scientific question development"
  - "multi-agent systems"
  - "dataset-grounded planning"
  - "scientific provenance"
